From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:13:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ec/lenovo/h8: Sleep on lid close under macOS on AC, where
 asked

On the ThinkPad W541 the panel is on DDI D, which macOS drives as an
external DisplayPort display (AppleDisplay, not AppleBacklightDisplay).
IOGraphics puts macOS in desktop mode whenever no built-in (backlight)
display is online, and IOPMrootDomain does not sleep on lid close in
desktop mode on AC (shouldSleepOnClamshellClosed()): closing the lid
then neither sleeps nor turns the panel off, which stays lit inside the
closed lid. On battery macOS sleeps on lid close as usual.

Let a board ask, with EC_LENOVO_H8_LID_SLEEP_DARWIN, for the sleep
button on a lid close event (_Q2B) under macOS (ISDW) on AC, as Fn+4
does through _Q13: macOS sleeps on it whatever the desktop mode. Not on
battery, where macOS sleeps by itself and the button would be a second
request. The wake on lid opening is armed in _PTS under macOS already.
The W541 asks for it; on the T440p macOS drives the panel as a built-in
display. Linux and Windows run the same _Q2B as before. With it, a lid
closed on AC always sleeps under macOS, also with an external display:
no clamshell mode.

TEST=Built lenovo/w541 with mrc.bin and with the native RAM init. In
acpiexec on its DSDT, with _OSI ("Darwin") answered, _Q2B notifies LID
and then SLPB (0x80) with the AC bit of the EC set, and LID only without
it; without "Darwin", and for _Q2A, LID only. The checks of the earlier
ACPI patches give the same results. Fn+4 (_Q13, the same notify of
SLPB) sleeps macOS 14 on the W541.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/ec.asl          | 11 +++++++++++
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/dsdt.asl |  4 ++++
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/ec.asl b/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/ec.asl
index 82b4c61a23..a340a99ab1 100644
--- a/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/ec.asl
+++ b/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/ec.asl
@@ -200,6 +200,17 @@ Device(EC)
 	Method(_Q2B, 0, NotSerialized)
 	{
 		Notify(^LID, 0x80)
+#ifdef EC_LENOVO_H8_LID_SLEEP_DARWIN
+		/*
+		 * The lid closed. macOS does not sleep on that in desktop mode on
+		 * AC, and it is in desktop mode whenever no built-in display is
+		 * online: on boards where it drives the panel as an external
+		 * display, press the sleep button for it on AC, as Fn+4 does.
+		 */
+		If (HPAC && \ISDW ()) {
+			Notify(^SLPB, 0x80)
+		}
+#endif
 	}
 
 
diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/dsdt.asl b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/dsdt.asl
index d959faad0c..1721a5356e 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/dsdt.asl
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/dsdt.asl
@@ -6,6 +6,10 @@
 #define THINKPAD_EC_WAKE_GPE 0x1d /* GPIO13 */
 #define EC_LENOVO_H8_ALT_FN_F2F3_LAYOUT 1
 #define EC_LENOVO_H8_FN_F9_F12_LAYOUT 1
+#if CONFIG(BOARD_LENOVO_THINKPAD_W541)
+/* macOS drives the panel, on DDI D, as an external display */
+#define EC_LENOVO_H8_LID_SLEEP_DARWIN 1
+#endif
 
 #include <acpi/acpi.h>
 DefinitionBlock(
